# E212: Python package pip/python3 not found in Conan build environment
# Contributor: C48A
# Status: draft

error_signature: pip: inaccessible or not found|python3: inaccessible or not found|Error 127 while executing
match_keywords: pip,python3,inaccessible,not found,ConanException,Error 127,python package,setuptools
root_cause: Conan build environment uses /bin/sh which does not have pip or python3 in PATH. The system python3 is installed at a non-standard path (e.g. /storage/Users/currentUser/.harmonybrew/opt/python@3.14/bin/python3.14). When conanfile.py build() or test_package test() calls self.run("pip install ...") or self.run("python3 -c ..."), /bin/sh cannot find these executables.
category: L2
severity: blocking
build_system: python
rec_description: Use sys.executable to get the full path to the Python interpreter, then use it with -m pip for pip commands. In conanfile.py build(): python_exe = sys.executable; self.run(f'{python_exe} -m pip install ...'). In test_package/conanfile.py test(): python_exe = sys.executable; self.run(f'{python_exe} -c "import mypackage"').
rec_command: python_exe = sys.executable; self.run(f'{python_exe} -m pip install --break-system-packages ...')
affected_scope: All pure Python packages packaged with Conan on OpenHarmony/OHOS platform (internetarchive, and any future Python packages)
verification_cmd: python3 $SKILL_ROOT/scripts/ohc-run.py conan-verify internetarchive 5.10.1
rec_priority: high
